{"decision":"edit", "issues":[{"quote":"draw the body upward into the shredder gap", "problem":"The drum is being pulled inward/into the machine, not 'upward' (which is ambiguous or incorrect given the rotated frame and the crushing action)."},{"quote":"turn steadily inside the rotors", "problem":"The drum is not just turning; it is actively being crushed, flattened, and consumed by the rotors."}], "caption":"The video captures a rotated shredder scene, with two interlocking toothed metal rotors beside a concrete floor, a red plate, and the corner logo. A light green and white drum, already rust smudged and dented, rests diagonally across the rotor gap. The rotors turn continuously, and the drum's left edge is pressed into the teeth, while a person in a light shirt and dark shorts stands partly visible at the lower edge, wearing a white glove and watching the machine from the right side.

The left side of the drum folds inward into a deep crease as the metal yields to the rotating teeth. The upper teeth grip the rim and draw the body inward into the shredder gap. The open top bends over, and the cylinder collapses into a curved, flattened shell. The person remains beside the machine, hand near the edge, while the drum continues to be crushed and pulled into the rotors.

The visible portion shows the drum still gripped, partly flattened, and held in the shredder's teeth during the ongoing shredding process.", "length_note":""}
